# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_rename_completeness_enumeration.py" "RENAME-COMPLETENESS ENUMERATION GATE: PASS" "rename completeness enumeration" "rename completeness enumeration (integration-audit P1 root-of-root: a STRUCTURAL invariant tying the set of repo-COORDINATE-keyed tables to the rename mover's coverage so the NEXT new repo-keyed table cannot silently reopen the rename-ORPHAN gap [it already fired for co_change, then for the CONSENT layer workspace_member + repo-scoped grant]. Introspects pg_attribute for EVERY core.* table carrying a repo column and asserts via pg_get_functiondef that _migrate_repo_coordinate re-points each, modulo a documented RETAIN allowlist [event = append-only audit history honest about the name-at-the-time; webhook_delivery = transient age-pruned inbox buffer]; plus allowlist hygiene [no typo'd or dead retain entry]. A new repo-keyed table lands red until consciously wired into the rename move or retained on purpose)" "rename completeness enumeration / coordinate-move completeness (catalog-introspecting structural gate: the rename mover re-points ALL repo-keyed tables modulo a documented retain allowlist; the next new repo-keyed table can't silently orphan on a rename; MOAT/CONSENT-critical)" 30
